{
  "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
  "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose that the -\u00ad the Georgia Supreme Court in this case had issued an order saying we affirm the decision below; our decision should not be taken as necessarily agreeing or disagreeing with the reasoning in the lower court's opinion. Would look-through be appropriate in that situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: You can't say?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose -- suppose that there is a decision by a state intermediate court of appeals, and the majority rejects a claim for certain reasons, and there's a concurrence in the judgment that says we would also reject the claim -- or I would also reject the claim for a different reason, and then that decision is summarily affirmed by the state supreme court. What happens there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "At what point does it become, would\nyou say, okay, well, that's enough, it's\nreasonable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Now, Richter does\nrequire a habeas court, a federal habeas court\nto imagine all of the conceivable arguments\nthat could have supported a state court\ndecision, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I'm not sure I\nunderstand the question. But suppose you said\nthat the reasoned decision is -- is not -- is\njust completely wrong."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right? Could the state come in with a totally new argument that wasn't made to the state court at all and say you should deny habeas on this totally new argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So why do we bother having state habeas anymore? Why don't we just say don't -- have federal habeas only and -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Where is the question of -- of Georgia law that is implicated here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "5c6312c5bd86b2097b751989bbe32fb8163429a819a4333d590222b3d9ee7441",
      "evidence_id": "ev-5c6312c5bd86-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the summary affirmance of the Georgia Supreme Court should not be treated the exact opposite as the way this Court and other federal courts treat their own summary affirmances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-6855",
